id: reflect
name: Reflect
type: outOfSequence
actionCost: 0
kiCostPerTier: 5
attacking: true
requiresTarget: true
reflect: true
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Turn an Energy or Magic attack around. Offered when a Parry avoids one, or when a
  Deflect or Distant Deflect wins its Might Clash; you roll Strike with their
  Profile and they roll the Wound Roll, Ki Wager and Energy Charges and all.
text: >
  Reflect Maneuver: Throw back an attack against an opponent!
  –Maneuver Type: Out-of-Sequence
  –Action Cost: N/A
  –KP Cost: 5(T)
  –Effect: If you avoid an Attacking Maneuver (that did not possess an AoE) due to
  using the Parry option of the Defend Maneuver or succeed at the Might Clash for
  the Deflect or Distant Deflect options of the Intervene Maneuver, you may use
  this Maneuver if the Attacking Maneuver was of the Energy or Magic Foundation.
  Roll Strike against an Opponent of your choice using the Profile of the initial
  Attacking Maneuver. If they are hit, the original attacking Opponent rolls the
  Wound Roll for their initial Attacking Maneuver instead as an Urgent Roll,
  including any Ki Wagers and Energy Charges included on that Attacking Maneuver.
  Damage calculation occurs as usual from this point.

---

# No script. An Out-of-Sequence Maneuver is never used from a list: it exists only
# as a chance something that just happened handed you, and that is the offer
# machinery rather than anything a script can reach. `reflect: true` hands it to the
# code, as `exploit` does for the Basic Attack that Maneuver gives away.
#
# Where the offer comes from, which is the whole of the "if" in the entry:
#   - the Parry option of the Defend Maneuver, where the Parry won and the attack
#     was avoided
#   - the Deflect and Distant Deflect options of the Intervene Maneuver, where the
#     Might Clash was won - the two the Intervene file marks `clashes`
#   - in both cases only when the attack was Energy or Magic and its Profile had no
#     Area of Effect
#
# "An Opponent of your choice" is a target you pick, not the one who threw it: the
# entry says any Opponent, so the token you have targeted is the one it goes to.
#
# --- The half of this that is new ------------------------------------------------
#
# "The original attacking Opponent rolls the Wound Roll for their initial Attacking
# Maneuver instead." One attack, two characters: you roll the Strike and they roll
# the Wound. Nothing here had ever split those - every attack in the system was one
# person's from the declaration to the Damage - so an attack now says who owes its
# Wound Roll where that is not the one who made it, and the button appears on their
# client rather than on yours.
#
# What they roll is their attack rather than a fresh one: their Wound, their Ki
# Wager, their Energy Charges, their Profile's own additions. So the reflected
# attack carries those across whole rather than working them out again from the
# Profile - a Beam's free Energy Charge is on that attack once, and deriving it a
# second time would hand it to them twice.
#
# "As an Urgent Roll", which in this system means a roll that cannot be failed on
# purpose - the option is closed with the reason beside it, as Compelled closes it.
#
# --- What the KP Cost is -----------------------------------------------------------
#
# "KP Cost: 5(T)", and nothing else. An attack ordinarily pays its Profile's cost
# too, and this one does not: the entry prices the Maneuver outright, and the Profile
# was paid for by whoever threw it the first time.
